    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20526" root="سلك" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسْلَكٌ</span></b>  [<i>A place of passage</i> of a man or beast
and of anything;] <i>a way, road,</i> or <i>path:</i> pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسَالِكُ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسْلَكَا المَرْأَةِ</span> [<i>The
vagina and rectum of the woman</i>]. (M in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فيض</span>. [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفَاضَ المَرْأَةَ</span> in that art.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [Hence,
also,] one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُذْ فِى مَسَالِكِ الحَقِّ</span> (tropical:)  [<i>Enter
thou upon the ways of truth</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِلْكٌ</span>.

